Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["RandomInfraParallel", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"2b61e889-1923-41da-b1e8-c1d7be851654"],

Cell["LLM generated.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2c8fe39d-3d0e-4a51-a8bd-3a6c71aab049"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"0509ff67-f284-41d3-bfdd-dc9b552275d2"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraParallel"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraParallel", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d34689e0-29cc-4d65-9c4f-8ab031e8a9a1"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives one parallel to ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] a shortest path through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " that stays at the distance ",
 StyleBox["d(p, line)", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " and cannot be prolonged at that distance \[LongDash] as a directed path \
graph.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"53678ae1-2b8f-4a2f-97ac-155df1bb4fa8"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraParallel"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraParallel", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "449f0c28-6fd3-4e0c-80cd-3c55c19fbcdc"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "573dda38-2fe0-43da-8d6b-381cb291e132"],
 " of exactly ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " parallels or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d2c2973-1ffa-4782-80c6-b6ee8ce2765f"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"UpTo", "[", "n", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "da7055a4-8c76-4edc-a00d-537132098902"],
 " gives up to ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0ef6980-100c-4261-bb7a-bd68dcfa53b5"],
 " gives the whole class as a pool of DAGs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"fbf9b73a-964c-422c-a659-5ed0b381fff2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The default draw is random. Seed with ",
 Cell[BoxData["SeedRandom"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0536734e-1956-4e98-a4cb-b33d3d95c2c5"],
 " to reproduce it. Give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<NextVertexFunction\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "Identity"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8a6532d6-d3d7-42c6-89ad-52dd5d37d934"],
 " for deterministic descent. ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "915379fe-046e-42f7-a4a7-11f502542c3a"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData["Automatic"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c8f493a-39d4-435e-9251-386d08271f91"],
 " keeps the full enumeration without drawing."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f0c064ed-bb1c-43d0-9208-d2068d026dcd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " for the level set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"l", "i", "n", "e"}], "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"l", "i", "n", "e"}], "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "edc4e87a-87f7-46d9-99ba-39a19f8ee93b"],
 ". A parallel to ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is a shortest path ",
 StyleBox["s \[Ellipsis] p \[Ellipsis] e", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] so ",
 StyleBox["d(s, e) = d(s, p) + d(p, e)", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] with every vertex in ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 ", such that no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " prolongs it. This reads Euclid's fifth postulate intrinsically: constant \
distance is what a metric can say about parallelism without a notion of \
direction. Inextensibility is measured inside ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 ", not in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", so a parallel need not be a line of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7dbda24b-67d7-4918-8cc5-305d1e0b24f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " is a vertex sequence, a walk graph, or a list of walk graphs, which \
spreads over its walks. Each parallel appears once, oriented so that ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " precedes ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " in canonical order."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bbb13e37-ed71-46ff-8676-ddff87db1e12"],

Cell["\<\
On the square grid the classical picture survives: through a vertex of a \
parallel row there is exactly one parallel to a row, and it is the row. Off a \
line that bends, the level set bends with it, and a shortest path inside it \
soon has to leave \[LongDash] the parallels are then few and short. Below, \
through a vertex at distance 2 from a line through the centre, the square \
tiling has one parallel of 10 edges beside a line of 24, the irregular mesh \
two, of 4 and 5 edges, the hexagonal tiling a single edge. A vertex with no \
neighbour in its level set has no parallel at all: the class is empty, not \
the one-vertex walk.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f6d0ed62-8e52-49dc-b38a-34b9a2e535e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraParallelQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraParallelQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0430ad55-a54a-45e9-9b77-a7437015e78d"],
 " asks a different question, and the two do not match. The predicate tests \
that two vertex sets are disjoint and at constant distance, and does not \
require either to be a shortest path. So it accepts pairs this function never \
returns \[LongDash] concentric shells, for instance, are parallel by that \
test \[LongDash] while every parallel returned here passes it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"78bf4ded-15bc-4367-97eb-8235335b62e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The class is carried by a ",
 StyleBox["pool",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": one shortest path DAG per admissible pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "), the ",
 StyleBox["s \[RightArrow] p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["p \[RightArrow] e", "TI"],
 " intervals cut down to ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " and glued at ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09066908-3292-4e08-981f-449bf9709ec8"],
 " returns the pool itself \[LongDash] a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b620ef54-f0eb-4d0f-baba-de15c1eeca96"],
 " of DAGs, a single atom giving the one DAG. A bounded count streams \
parallels off the atoms as directed path graphs, and the count-less call is \
one random parallel."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8163019f-7006-46ed-83ae-d4fe45f970eb"],

